ents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> I see we have a \"wrong type\" test but do we have a \"correct type\" test?\r\n\r\nThe \"wrong type\" test is an indicator of the \"correct type\" test since it should give that specific error if it's not the correct type. And the test should also fail if `Color` is being treated as a correct type somehow. So they're opposites, basically! (Not polar opposites since the test can fail for different reasons too, but sorta.) Therefore, probably not necessary to add a new test. (Even if it was, that's probably out of scope for this PR since I just needed to adjust the tests for this PR to work.)","created_at":"2026-08-02T10:12:46Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T10:12:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121684#discussion_r3698663209","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121684","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3698663209"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121684#discussion_r3698663209"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121684"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3698663209/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3694647849,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"}]